Build a complete retro arcade Snake game in HTML/CSS/JavaScript with neon aesthetic in a single HTML file on a 480x480 canvas.

**Core Gameplay:**
- 20×20 grid with 24px cells
- Snake starts center-aligned with 3 segments facing right
- Arrow keys or WASD to control direction; support both simultaneously
- Input buffer holds up to 2 queued moves; prevent 180° turns and duplicate inputs
- Food spawns randomly in empty cells; collision adds 1 segment and scores 10 points
- Speed increases each food: start at 150ms per move, subtract 4ms per food (min 55ms)
- Death on wall collision or self-collision (tail is safe if growing that frame)
- P key toggles pause/resume

**Power-Ups:**
- Two power-up types: Yuzu Berry (yellow/green orb) and Ghost Star (white 5-point star with cyan glow)
- Power-ups spawn randomly every 6–13 seconds, exist for 9 seconds before disappearing
- **Yuzu Berry (Slow-Mo):** Multiplies tick interval by 1.8× for 6 seconds; grab for yellow beep sound
- **Ghost Star:** Allows snake to phase through itself for 6 seconds; grab for ascending triple beep (740→990→1240 Hz)
- Power-up HUD badges display active effects with countdown timers (format: "0.0s"); badges blink when <1.5s remain
- Yuzu badge: yellow circle on yellow border; Ghost badge: white circle on cyan border

**Visual Style (Neon Arcade):**
- Dark background (#05050a); use "Press Start 2P" for chunky retro font
- Neon palette: green (#39ff14), pink (#ff2ec4), cyan (#00f0ff), yellow (#ffee00)
- Canvas: glowing cyan border with box-shadow glow, dark interior
- Faint cyan grid overlay; Snake head cyan with glow, body fades to green with decreasing opacity
- Chunky pixel eyes (4×4px) on head, positioned by direction
- Food: pulsing pink diamond (pulse 180ms, scale 0.72–0.88)
- Yuzu: yellow orb (bobbing up/down) with green leaf; Ghost: white star with cyan glow (bobbing, rotating)
- Ghost mode colors: head white, body cyan, reduced opacity with shimmer
- Partial canvas clearing (32% opacity dark fill) creates neon motion trails

**Effects & Feedback:**
- Particle burst (14 pink/yellow radiating particles, ~450ms) on food and power-up eat
- Screen shake on death: 420ms decay, random offset up to ±10px
- Death animation: 650ms flashing (80ms intervals) red/white segments
- Audio: start (660Hz, 880Hz), food (pitch rises with score), death (220→140→80Hz sawtooth descending)

**Persistent State & UI:**
- localStorage high score under 'neonSnakeHiScore'
- HUD: score (green glow, left), power-up badges (center), hi-score (pink glow, right)
- Start overlay: pulsing "NEON SNAKE" title (green+pink), "INSERT COIN" button (yellow, blinking), control hints
- Pause overlay: "PAUSED" title, hints about power-up effects, "PRESS P TO RESUME" prompt
- Game Over overlay: final score, best score, "NEW HI-SCORE" badge (if applicable)
- CRT scanlines overlay across entire page (subtle 3px dark lines)

**States & Input:**
- States: 'start', 'playing', 'paused', 'dying' (650ms), 'gameover'
- Space/Enter starts from start/game-over screens; arrow/WASD auto-starts from start screen
- P toggles pause; pause freezes rendering but power-up timers continue counting down
- Click overlays to interact (start button, game-over screen to restart, pause screen to resume)
